{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/250586-alternative-botch-idea-brainstorming","id":250586,"title":"Alternative Botch Idea [Brainstorming]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-09-06T01:23:10-07:00","id":250586,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Alternative Botch Idea [Brainstorming]","content":"So, I've been mulling over a few thoughts on various cWOD systems as I've been mildly working on my own personal &quot;cWOD 4e.&quot;<br /> <br /> One of the things that's always been a bit of an issue with the cWOD mechanics is the Rule of 1s. They make the math of the dice fairly funky, they have a habit of feeling like they punish you for having high stats, and just in general make it hard to feel safe with your stats because it is so easy to loose successes to those 1s.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, I most certainly don't want to go to the Exalted/etc. level of botches being trivially easy to ignore, or the nWOD level of dramatic failures only happening in the most rare of circumstances or at player discretion.<br /> <br /> So, here's what I've been thinking:<br /> <br /> 1s no long subtract successes.<br /> <br /> Instead the number of 1s you roll are compared to two numbers. You successes rolled, and the lowest trait used to create the dice-pool.<br /> <br /> If the roll is successful, and you roll a number of 1s equal to or greater to your successes on the roll you gain a minor complication.<br /> If the roll is successful, and you roll a number of 1s equal to or greater to your lowest trait involved you gain a complication.<br /> If the roll fails and you roll any 1s, you gain a complication.<br /> If the roll fails and you roll equal to or greater than you lowest trait involved, you gain a major complication.<br /> <br /> You only apply one complication from a roll, and always the worst. So if you have Dexterity 3 and Brawl 2 and roll to attack, and get two successes and two 1s, you gain a complication. Not a minor complication and a complication. Or stacking them for a major complication.<br /> <br /> Minor complications do not directly interfere with the action taken, but will often result in a penalty to your next action or result in a small amount of time to deal with (ex: gun jams that require an action to clear).<br /> Normal complications can reduce the impact of a successful roll but generally result a significant narrative obstacle that will make capitalizing on the initial action more difficult (ex: You successfully hit on a woman in the bar enough that she's interested, only for her boyfriend to show up and now very angry).<br /> Major complications are a more traditional botch that represents completely screwing something up beyond any immediate hope of salvaging it (hence they only happen on natural failures)<br /> <br /> Thoughts?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-06T09:38:34-07:00","id":250819,"title":"","content":"I'm planning to use a Paradox-like stat, &quot;misluck&quot; (so, this system is still incomplete), used only on normal, mundane actions (not related to Disciplines/Gifts/WhateverMagic or Virtues/Paths/etc)<br /> for example:<br /> ACCUMULATING MISLUCK<br /> -. Gianni the Giovanni shot a gun, 2 success and 2 &quot;1&quot;. It's a plain unsuccess, but the action would succeed if not for the 1's, I count the action as a &quot;limitately successful&quot; and take note of the 1's. Now said players has 2 misluck point, but sht gun shoot anyway.<br /> -. then the player, while chasing a car, roll 1 success and 2 &quot;1&quot;. Would be a botch, but but the action would still succeed if not for the &quot;1&quot;. I secretely roll a dice, if I get &quot;1&quot; the Misluk <i>Discharge</i>, if it's not a &quot;1&quot;, I add to his Misluck bill, 3 points (2 for the 1's + 1 for the botch). Let's say I get a &quot;4&quot;. The action is &quot;limitately successful&quot; and his Misluck is now 5 points strong.<br /> -. in the end our poor Giovanni, try to shot again at his defenseless target. Only one &quot;1&quot; and not successes. It's a plain botch, and the action wouldn't succeed even if you do not count the &quot;1&quot;. I add the &quot;misluck points&quot; to his bill, and the action fail. Now, he has 6 misluck points. The botch with no successes cause always a <i>Discharge</i>.<br /> <br /> DISCHARGE<br /> The Misluck accumulated by the player simply discharge all in one action.<br /> I compare the character's Misluck bill with a chart (I'm still making).<br /> -. Let's say that, at level 5 there is a &quot;minor mechanical trouble&quot;, I subtract 5 points from his Misluck bill. The gun jam. He has still 1 Misluck point.<br /> -. If the character had, like, 10 Misluck points, that would be a &quot;major mechanical trouble&quot;. The gun would probably be irreparably marred, with no side effects.<br /> -. If the character had, like, 20 Misluck points, that would be a &quot;critical mechanical trouble&quot;. The gun would explode, inflicting actual damage to the poor character.<br /> [this section is still in the making, but that's the general idea]<br /> <br /> VENTING MISLUCK<br /> -. At the end of a play session, all Misluck bills go down by 1.<br /> -. If there is downtime between sessions, the bills go down by 5.<br /> -. At the end of a story, all the bills go to 0.<br /> <br /> <br /> As a sidenote, these calculations are best kept away from the players.<br /> So you can alter the bills if the results could harm your chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ed6RV6Z.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","name":"Ryoga84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}